{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Until its produce comes.</b> The designation 'its produce' refers to the eighth year, not the ninth. And the measure of the verse is thus: 'And you shall sow in the eighth year, and you shall eat of the old produce until its produce comes' — and it will suffice for you until the ninth year. And when it says 'for three years,' they are not three complete years, for they are: part of the sixth year, and the entire seventh year when they do not sow, and part of the eighth year. Thus explained the sage R. Abraham, of blessed memory."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:22.406074730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}